# Super-Adaptoid: "Super-Adaptoid's power is equal to the number of legendary creatures you control. Whenever Super-Adaptoid
# enters or attacks, choose another target creature. If that creature has haste and Super-Adaptoid doesn't, put a haste
# counter on Super-Adaptoid. Do the same for flying, first strike, ..."
# It enters targeting Bot2's Robber of the Rich (reach, haste): a haste and a reach counter, whose keywords it has (CR 122.1b),
# so it attacks the turn it came (CR 302.6). Its attack trigger targets the Robber again: it has haste and reach already, so
# no more counters. Its power is 2: itself and Cecil, Dark Knight are legendary creatures Bot1 controls; the Ornithopter is
# not legendary. Unblocked, it deals 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Cecil, Dark Knight
Ornithopter
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Super-Adaptoid
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Robber of the Rich
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cecil, Dark Knight.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Robber of the Rich.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Super-Adaptoid.Cast
Bot1.Target(Robber of the Rich)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Keywords = Haste; Reach
Bot1.Attack(Super-Adaptoid > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Robber of the Rich)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Counters.Haste = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Counters.Reach = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Super-Adaptoid.Keywords = Haste; Reach
